# Nibs — agentic-first issue tracker

Use nibs (not TodoWrite or todo lists) for all work tracking in this project.

**Before using any `nibs` command, run `nibs prime --full` to load the full reference.** That command emits the complete CLI guide (commands, flags, body section conventions, GraphQL schema). Do not guess syntax — read the full reference first.

Tip: `nibs list --columns id,status,title` (and `nibs links --columns ...`) emits tab-separated rows for easy parsing — see `--full` for the full column set.

## Workflow

- BEFORE a task: find or create a nib (`nibs list --ready`, `nibs create "Title" -t <type>`), set status `in-progress`. (`--ready` excludes blocked, in-progress, completed, scrapped, draft, and `deferred`/parked nibs — see `--full` for status semantics.)
- DURING: keep todo items current (`- [ ]` → `- [x]`) as work happens.
- AFTER: mark `completed` only when no unchecked todos remain. Append `## Summary of Changes` (or `## Reasons for Scrapping`).
- COMMITS: include both code and nib files.
- SUBAGENTS: set `in-progress` BEFORE launching, `completed` AFTER — they run fresh and won't update nibs for you.

## Errors

If a `nibs` command errors, stop. Find the root cause and suggest a mitigation (code fix, follow-up nib, workaround). Never silently retry.
</EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>
